00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.460 align:start position:0%
 
you  a man who spent three decades in prison  for a murder he says he did not commit  could be a big step closer to freedom as  soon as tomorrow  Crossley Greene was found guilty of  shooting and killing 22 year old chip  Flynn in 1989 prosecutors relied on the  word of Flynn's former girlfriend Kim  Halleck  even though law enforcement thought she  might be the shooter Erin Moriarty who's  followed this case since 1999 for 48  hours spoke with green ahead of the  federal appeals court hearing my name is  cross Nick green I've been convicted for  a crime I didn't commit  31 years that's nothing to break him in  that's enough to destroy a man in the  early morning hours of April 4th 1989 22  year-old Charles Flynn known as chip was  found in a Florida orange grove with a  single bullet in his chest  still alive Flynn's former girlfriend  Kim Halleck told police that a black man  had robbed a couple hijacked them and  then shot Flynn I don't believe a word  she says Brevard County first responders  mark rixie and Sergeant diane clark  questioned why Halleck didn't  immediately call 9-1-1 instead she drove  to a friend's house something's wrong  here something is not ringing true more  surprising was what happened when they  found Flynn lucid and talking first  words out of his mouth were get me out  of here  did he mention anything about an  assailant  don't know I'm thinking what the hell is  going on here  Flynn was pronounced dead at the  hospital Hallett was never investigated  as the possible shooter even though she  admitted she had argued with Flynn who  has seen another woman instead  detectives arrested 31 year-old Crosley  Greene a small-time local drug dealer  and charged him with kidnapping robbery  and murder it was a total shock this was  like picking a name out of a hat  Halleck who said she didn't get a good  look at the assailant  pick greens photo from what his  attorneys say was a rigged line up cross  a greens picture is put in what is known  in investigative circles as the bullseye  because it's where your eyes naturally  go to first rixie and Clark now retired  went to the assistant state attorney  handling the case  Christopher White and told him they  believe Kim Halleck was the shooter  white took notes I reviewed all the  evidence that we had with that  hypotheses in line he spoke about that  meeting in 2015 do they give me cause to  believe that Kim Halleck may have  committed this murder my answer is No  prosecutors built their case around  three witnesses including green sister  Sheila who testified the green it  confessed to them Green was offered a  deal but he turned it down  I can't plead guilty to something I  didn't do on September 5th 1990 an  all-white jury convicted green but since  then Sheila green and the other  witnesses have recanted Green got his  biggest break when his attorneys  obtained something Christopher white  never intended them to see those notes  from the meeting with Mark Richt C and  Diane Clark mark and Diane suspect the  girl did it she changed her story a  couple of times also noticed she never  asked how the victim was in July 2018 a  federal judge ruled that withholding  those notes from Crosley green kept him  from getting a fair trial and he  reversed his conviction our Constitution  prohibits the government from hiding  evidence of innocence and that's what  happened here and yet because the state  of Florida is appealing Green is still  in prison  I want the truth to come out okay you  choose to this case is that I've been  locked up all these years for a crime I  didn't commit  hopefully I get that chance to go home  that's the truth  the Florida Attorney General's Office  says that it's unable to comment on this  pending case but in a brief filed last  year it called the federal courts  decision to reverse greens conviction  procedurally factually and legally  incorrect we've also reached out to Kim  Halleck in the former assistant state  attorney Christopher white who have not  responded to our request for comment I  would love to sit down with Kim Halleck  she has never spoken to me and I all she  has to do is kind of explain what  happened where is she now  she is living in titusville going on  with her life while of course right now  Carla Green is sitting in prison now  he's gonna get closer I think to having  a real decision here tomorrow morning  and I'll be there the federal appellate  court will hear oral arguments and if  the court rules in his favor  then he either has to get a new trial  within 60-90 days they'll have to decide  or let him go home Wow right we hope  justice will be served

